From 9ed7291245e57d3af412e7a667455c0053c9a4ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josh Lukens <jlukens@botch.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:08:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Listeners: fixes from review

- Correlate on insteon-mqtt's own clock (arrival), never the listener's:
  a listener clock that is off can no longer make a heard message look
  missed. The modem-heard window runs to the actual release time, so a
  release delayed by the main loop cannot miss a modem copy read
  meanwhile.
- Do not inject a message if the modem has since read a later message
  from the same device (a close after an open, the cleanup after a
  broadcast): that replayed old state.
- Group broadcasts the modem has no responder link for are not counted
  as missed and never injected (the modem would never pass them up).
- Reject non-finite 't' (NaN poisoned the TimedCall queue and stalled
  every timed call) and drop messages older than 10 s instead of
  re-dating them as fresh. 't' is now required.
- Rate limit per device per minute (4) instead of one per 30 s, so an
  open/close pair both get through; release oldest first.
- Protocol: drop the injected-copy guard. The modem's late copy of a
  message it missed almost never arrives, so the guard swallowed the
  next real identical press instead.

