From febd5c68452d8660dab026dbe4e6c342ba76519c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josh Lukens <jlukens@botch.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:23:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Listeners: findings and timing from the Fable review

- Cleanup status reports (0x06) are never injected and not counted as
  misses ('reports'): they carry no state, were ~85% of what the modem
  misses from battery devices, and each used a rate-limit slot.
- A modem read of the same bytes within 2 s on air counts as heard even
  if credited to another event (a device retransmits 0.5-1.4 s later);
  duplicate modem reads are not recorded (one could be credited to a
  later, missed, press).
- Broadcast/cleanup pairing is matched on on-air time within PAIR_S
  (8 s; measured gap p99 5.3 s) instead of the early window, which the
  cleanup path never reached.
- Leak sensors: groups 1 (dry) and 2 (wet) are one state for the
  'newer' rule.
- An exception deciding one event no longer strands the other due ones.
- EARLY_S 1.5 -> 2.5 s, MATCH_S 1.5 -> 2.0 s (measured lags).

